---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { plugins } from "../../data/plugins";
---
<Layout title="Plugin registry — Torana" description="Curated Torana plugins and their requested capability classes.">
  <section class="frame prose" style="max-width:var(--page)">
    <p class="eyebrow">Registry v1 · curated</p>
    <h1 class="display">Install behavior, not a starter pack.</h1>
    <p>Official plugins are adopted individually. The current registry indexes reviewed source projects and their requested capability classes. Torana binds operator approvals to the locally built WASM digest, so an artifact or permission change requires approval again.</p>
    <div class="catalog">
      {plugins.map((plugin) => (
        <article class="plugin">
          <h3>torana/{plugin.name}</h3>
          <p>{plugin.description}</p>
          <span class="tag">{plugin.kind}</span>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <h2>Registry API</h2>
    <pre><code>GET https://torana.sh/registry/v1/index.json</code></pre>
    <p>The registry is intentionally curated for v1. Automated release-bundle installation is not available yet; build official or personal plugins from source and configure the resulting local bundle explicitly.</p>
    <p><strong>The registry deliberately publishes no digests.</strong> A digest is only checkable if the same source builds to the same bytes everywhere, and Torana does not yet verify that across machines and toolchains. Publishing one we could not stand behind would train you to skip the comparison that matters. The digest you approve is the one <em>your</em> machine produced from source you can read — compare it against what the control plane shows, not against a number from this page.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
